{"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"Getting Started","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using SwiftData?"}]},{"text":" See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Develop with Claude Code","anchor":"Develop-with-Claude-Code","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/claude.com\/claude-code","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", install the Ensembles skill first. It teaches Claude the API, the cloud backends, Ensembles 2 → 3 migration, the seed policy, and the common pitfalls, so it writes correct setup code and diagnoses sync issues without hand-holding:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["\/plugin marketplace add mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3","\/plugin install ensembles@ensembles"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project","anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Ensembles package to your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3.git"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit","anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model","anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Xcode, add a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".xcdatamodeld"},{"text":" file to your project (e.g., ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Model.xcdatamodeld"}]},{"text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Note"},{"text":" entity with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"text":" (String) and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueID"},{"text":" (String) attributes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`","anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For deduplication, conform your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"text":" subclass to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A global identifier "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"must never change","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Set Up the Container","anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewContext"},{"text":" so your UI stays up to date.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Using a Custom Store Location","anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storeURL"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack","anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you already have an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentContainer"},{"text":", pass it in directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Or if you have an existing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObjectContext"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Auto-Sync Configuration","anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Control when syncing occurs with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"autoSyncPolicy"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".manual"},{"text":" and call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" yourself for full control over timing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2","anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".ensembles3"},{"text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble","text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Create and Attach","type":"heading","anchor":"Create-and-Attach","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Changes","anchor":"Sync-Changes"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)"},{"type":"text","text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Handle the Delegate","anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Implement ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate","type":"reference"},{"text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"aside","name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"text":" subclasses conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", you don’t need to implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects"},{"text":" — the ensemble discovers identifier properties automatically. You only need the delegate method if you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly without ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"tip"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other delegate methods let you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Inspect and repair merge data","type":"text"}]},{"text":" before it’s committed (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Handle save failures","type":"text"}]},{"text":" during merging (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"React to forced detaches","type":"text"}]},{"text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"didDetachWithError:"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution","type":"reference"},{"text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Detach","anchor":"Detach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Seed Policies","anchor":"Seed-Policies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy","type":"reference"},{"text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","isActive":true},{"text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","isActive":true},{"text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Options","anchor":"Sync-Options"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For advanced control, pass ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Process Pending Changes","anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()","type":"reference"},{"text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChange